(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Spanning Tree Protocol \(STP, IEEE 802.1D\). Explain why Layer 2 switching loops cause catastrophic broadcast storms, how the Root Bridge and port roles are elected, and the convergence state transitions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Catastrophic Impact of Layer 2 Switching Loops:) Tj
T*
(   To prevent network downtime from single cable or switch failures, network engineers build) Tj
T*
(   redundant physical links between switches.) Tj
T*
(   However, Layer 2 Ethernet frames contain NO Time-to-Live \(TTL\) hop limit counter.) Tj
T*
(   When a host broadcasts a frame \(such as an ARP request\), redundant switches forward the) Tj
T*
(   broadcast frame out of all ports indefinitely,) Tj
T*
(   creating a exponentially multiplying 'Broadcast Storm'.) Tj
T*
(   Consequences: 100% CPU saturation on switches, total MAC table thrashing \(CAM table) Tj
T*
(   instability\), and complete network collapse within seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Spanning Tree Protocol Algorithm \(Radia Perlman\):) Tj
T*
(   STP logically breaks physical loops by selectively placing redundant switch ports into a) Tj
T*
(   'Blocking' state while keeping active paths loop-free.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Elect the Root Bridge:) Tj
T*
(   Switches exchange Bridge Protocol Data Units \(BPDUs\). The switch with the lowest Bridge ID \(BID) Tj
T*
(   = Priority + MAC Address\) becomes the Root Bridge.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Determine Root Ports \(RP\):) Tj
T*
(   On every non-root switch, exactly one port with the lowest cumulative path cost to the Root) Tj
T*
(   Bridge is elected as the Root Port.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Determine Designated Ports \(DP\):) Tj
T*
(   On every physical network segment, the switch port providing the lowest path cost to the Root) Tj
T*
(   Bridge is designated as the Designated Port \(all ports on the Root Bridge are DPs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Block Redundant Ports \(Non-Designated Ports\):) Tj
T*
(   All remaining ports that are neither Root Ports nor Designated Ports are placed into the) Tj
T*
(   'Alternate / Blocking' state, eliminating loops.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Convergence Port States \(Legacy 802.1D\):) Tj
T*
(   - Blocking: Discards user frames; listens for BPDUs only \(prevents loops\).) Tj
T*
(   - Listening \(15s\): Prepares to forward; processes BPDUs to verify topology; does NOT learn MAC) Tj
T*
(   addresses.) Tj
T*
(   - Learning \(15s\): Populates MAC address table from incoming frames; does NOT yet forward) Tj
T*
(   frames.) Tj
T*
(   - Forwarding: Normal active operational state; forwards user frames and learns MAC addresses.) Tj
T*
(   - Disabled: Administratively shut down.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
